# Tutorial 21 — Reactive UI and Facets
# Reference: docs/guides/vns-by-example/11-reactive-ui-and-facets.md
# Read scripts/tutorial/README.md for the complete course and linked references.
@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_tutorial_21
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}
{{BG_DECL}}@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[set ui.textBoxAsset none]
[set ui.continueIndicator spinning_arrow]
[if tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion true]
[else]
[set ui.reduceMotion false]
[endif]
[if !tutorial_initialized]
[set tutorial_count 0]
[flag tutorial_initialized]
[endif]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.5]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.5]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
{{BG_START}}
[textspeed 28]
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Menus handle navigation. Facets and overlay screens handle story-facing interfaces such as a status card, inventory view, or confirmation panel.
@label lesson_menu
> Open a live workshop card -> demo
> Understand bindings and return values -> model
> Build your own interface -> practice
> Checkpoint -> checkpoint
> Finish and return to the hub -> return_hub
@label demo
[set workshop_energy 0.4]
[set workshop_name Lavender]
[screen show tutorial_card]
Lavender: The card reads variables while it renders. Its bar currently shows 40 percent.
[set workshop_energy 0.8]
Lavender: Now the same card shows 80 percent. I changed a variable; I did not rebuild the interface.
[screen hide tutorial_card]
Lavender: Next is a modal call. Use a button on the card to return to this conversation.
[screen call tutorial_card]
Lavender: The return value was {b}${screen.return.tutorial_card}{/b}.
[jump lesson_menu]
@label model
Lavender: Open {b}config/facets/tutorial_card.facet{/b}. Its text and bar read variables; its buttons return stable IDs.
Lavender: {b}screen show{/b} leaves the story running. {b}screen call{/b} waits for a return action. A called screen needs an exit, including when an optional button is disabled.
Lavender: Nodes can be text, images, bars, or groups. Parent groups establish coordinates; paint order, visibility conditions, and enabled conditions determine what the player can use.
Lavender: Keep state in VNS variables and appearance in the facet. That makes save/load, localization, and testing easier to reason about.
[jump lesson_menu]
@label practice
Lavender: Add a second bar and a warning that appears only when energy is low. Add a conditional button, but keep Close available in every state.
Lavender: Exercise: set energy below and above the threshold, use the screen with keyboard and pointer, then test a long translated label and large font scale.
Lavender: For reusable visual patterns, explore facets and motifs in the guide linked from the workshop README.
[jump lesson_menu]
@label checkpoint
Lavender: Which command waits for a modal screen to return a result?
> screen call -> correct
> screen show -> retry
@label retry
Lavender: Show is non-blocking. Call waits for the screen's return action.
[jump checkpoint]
@label correct
Lavender: Right. Always make that return action reachable.
[jump return_hub]

@label return_hub
[screen hide tutorial_card]
[if !tutorial_done_21]
[flag tutorial_done_21]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[goto {{HUB_TARGET}}:topics_page_4]
